Subject: Spell XGETBV as an instruction instead of raw opcode bytes
Origin: Filnix
Upstream-Status: Not submitted

Fil-C validates inline instructions and supports xgetbv with these register
constraints. Raw .byte directives cannot be validated, so every call that
dispatched to an optimized implementation stopped the program.

--- a/lib/x86/cpu_features.c
+++ b/lib/x86/cpu_features.c
@@ -65,7 +65,7 @@
 	 * This must be 'volatile' to prevent this code from being moved out
 	 * from under the check for OSXSAVE.
 	 */
-	__asm__ volatile(".byte 0x0f, 0x01, 0xd0" :
+	__asm__ volatile("xgetbv" :
 			 "=d" (d), "=a" (a) : "c" (index));
 
 	return ((u64)d << 32) | a;
